WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:05.240
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.540
This is the story of their lives and adventures.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.510
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.760
Oh, Koharu!

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:37.560
This is where they hold
the Pokémon Circus.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:40.560
Wow!
It’s the very image of a circus!

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.730
Yeah. Ready to go, then?

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.360
I’m feeling nervous...

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:52.370
This circus hosts very popular, spectacular performances
featuring Pokémon and their partners.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:01:00.040
Satoshi and Go were chosen by lottery
to be guest stars in a circus show today.

00:01:01.920 --> 00:01:04.130
Hello!

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:07.050
They’re so high up!

00:01:07.050 --> 00:01:08.630
Wow!

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.010
It’s an Eevee!

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:14.970
Now!

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:26.860
Nice jump, Karen!

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:29.610
Let’s go!

00:01:31.530 --> 00:01:32.490
Come on!

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.740
Whoa!

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:41.040
That was amazing, right, Eevee?

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:26.350
Circuses are <i>enchanting!</i>

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:29.520
Welcome, on your fleeting visit
to a world of dreams!

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:33.280
You are Satoshi and Go,
correct?

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.610
Huh? Expedition leader?

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.820
No, it’s the president from
the Fossil Museum!

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:43.120
<i>Non, non!</i>
I am the ringleader of this circus!

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.370
Call me “Ringleader!”

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.670
Nice to meet you!

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:50.330
N-Nice to meet you...

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:52.550
How was it
watching them rehearse?

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:54.590
It got me really pumped!

00:03:54.590 --> 00:03:55.550
It was thrilling!

00:03:55.550 --> 00:03:57.300
Yes, yes.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:59.720
Thrills and chills
are what make circuses...

00:03:59.720 --> 00:04:02.140
<i>...enchanting!</i>

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.720
Um...

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:08.270
My name is Koharu.
I’m a friend of Satoshi and Go’s.

00:04:08.270 --> 00:04:10.560
May I watch the rehearsals, too?

00:04:10.560 --> 00:04:12.520
Of course!

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:18.030
I read the circus was going to star
Thunders and Booster,

00:04:18.030 --> 00:04:20.620
and I was hoping I might
get to meet them.

00:04:22.450 --> 00:04:24.410
What a happy coincidence!

00:04:24.410 --> 00:04:28.870
You see, those two Eevee
are just about ready to evolve.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:31.920
Allow me to introduce you!

00:04:32.460 --> 00:04:35.880
These are Honoka and Billy,
members of my circus.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:39.970
They’ll be the final act of the circus,
the flying trapeze.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.050
Nice to meet you!
My name’s Honoka!

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:45.470
A performer who loves
Fire types!

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.980
She’s my partner, Karen.

00:04:49.890 --> 00:04:51.270
I’m Billy.

00:04:51.270 --> 00:04:54.320
A performer who loves nothing more
than Electric types.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:56.860
This is my partner, Rhyme.

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:02.910
Fire-type acts are cool, and get you fired up!
Nothing’s more popular!

00:05:03.910 --> 00:05:06.540
Fire types are past their prime.

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:10.160
Electric types are
the future number one.

00:05:10.670 --> 00:05:15.800
The two of them are always going at it
over which of them is the top star.

00:05:16.210 --> 00:05:18.170
So they’re rivals?!

00:05:18.170 --> 00:05:20.130
That’s why sparks are flying
between them...

00:05:22.930 --> 00:05:27.640
You two, will you let Koharu here
watch you evolve your Eevee?

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.270
Course! No problem!

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:34.480
I just got the evolution stone
I needed for this show, after all.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:39.360
The evolution stone I asked my friend
to get me just arrived, too!

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:43.660
I’ll evolve Eevee into Booster
with this Fire Stone,

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:46.120
and put on an even more
powerful show!

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:51.040
I’ll evolve my Eevee into Thunders
with this Thunder Stone,

00:05:51.040 --> 00:05:53.460
and put together a show
like nothing you’ve ever seen!

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:56.960
Hey! I’m going first,
so don’t you go butting in!

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:59.710
<i>You’re</i> the one in <i>my</i> way!
I’ll go first!

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:01.130
I’m going first!

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.220
No, I am!

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:02.930
What’s wrong with you?

00:06:02.930 --> 00:06:04.220
What’s the problem?

00:06:04.220 --> 00:06:05.680
Okay, Karen!

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:07.350
Here goes, Rhyme!

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:16.190
N-No way...?!

00:06:28.700 --> 00:06:32.410
Thunders! Lightning Pokémon!
Electric type!

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.370
They send out electrical charges
of about 10,000 volts!

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:39.130
Because they are high-strung,
it can be difficult to grow close to them!

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:45.590
Booster! Fire Pokémon!
Fire type!

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:52.980
It stores some of the air it inhales in its internal flame pouch,
which heats it to 1,700 degrees!

00:06:54.600 --> 00:07:00.650
My Karen... turned into
the Electric-type Thunders...

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:07.280
My Rhyme... became
the Fire type, Booster?

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.990
Y-You have to be kidding me!

00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.990
What am I gonna do now?!

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.580
This is your fault, you know!

00:07:12.580 --> 00:07:13.910
You kidding me?! <i>You</i> did this!

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:16.120
Let’s try again
with the spare stone...

00:07:16.120 --> 00:07:17.960
Once over, from the top!

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:25.630
It’s not working?! How come?!

00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:26.720
No way! This can’t be real!
What do I do now?!

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:26.720
Now what do I do?!

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:28.800
Pull yourselves together!

00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:35.640
But we can’t do the
flying trapeze of fire like this!

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:39.650
I’d been planning an
Electric performance, too!

00:07:39.650 --> 00:07:41.230
Hmm...

00:07:41.230 --> 00:07:45.990
If you can’t do the act,
that is troubling...

00:07:45.990 --> 00:07:47.410
Oh, I know!

00:07:47.410 --> 00:07:48.950
We don’t have much time
until the show,

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:52.910
so why don’t you
swap your Pokémon?

00:07:56.290 --> 00:07:57.540
What?!

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:59.920
Swapping their partners?!

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:01.590
Think about
how the Pokémon’ll feel!

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:08.050
If it’s just for this show,
then so be it.

00:08:08.050 --> 00:08:11.050
We’re professional performers,
after all.

00:08:11.050 --> 00:08:13.180
The show must go on.

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.970
We have to give it a try.

00:08:17.230 --> 00:08:18.440
Hmph!

00:08:22.060 --> 00:08:23.900
Are they gonna be okay?

00:08:23.900 --> 00:08:25.280
Who knows...

00:08:25.280 --> 00:08:28.360
I must apologize
for all this arguing.

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.280
Now, let’s get you practicing!

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:31.660
Right!

00:08:31.660 --> 00:08:34.790
Let’s see,
the two of you could...

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.380
Pikachu!

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:51.840
Pikachu! 100,000 Volts!

00:09:08.280 --> 00:09:09.820
Sarunori! Branch Jab!

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.660
That looks hard...

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:23.000
No, no! Start over!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:26.210
It’s 3, 2, 1, jump!

00:09:27.210 --> 00:09:29.130
Are you listening? Rhyme!

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:32.130
Really...
You have to concentrate!

00:09:34.640 --> 00:09:37.810
Karen, you’ve gotta use Thunder Shock
when I give the signal.

00:09:37.810 --> 00:09:39.640
How many times
do I have to tell you?

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:42.600
This is useless.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:44.730
She won’t listen to a word I say.

00:09:44.730 --> 00:09:47.070
We can’t rehearse anything like this.

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:03.960
Even when you evolve,
you’d want to stay by your partner’s side...

00:10:06.540 --> 00:10:08.460
Pocket Monsters!

00:10:20.270 --> 00:10:22.140
Fire team, assemble!

00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:26.230
Everyone, use Ember!

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:36.160
Wha—?

00:10:36.160 --> 00:10:38.450
Karen...
Why are you here?

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.620
What’s wrong?

00:10:40.620 --> 00:10:43.370
Shouldn’t you be rehearsing
with Billy?

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:53.010
Come on! Thunder Shock!

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:00.810
What?

00:11:01.560 --> 00:11:03.230
If it isn’t Rhyme...

00:11:04.230 --> 00:11:05.640
What’s up?

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:08.360
Aren’t you supposed to be
rehearsing with Honoka?

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:17.320
Hmm... Is that so...?

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:22.870
So Karen and Rhyme aren’t
accepting the partner swap?

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:24.330
Right.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:25.790
Hey, Karen...

00:11:25.790 --> 00:11:28.540
I’ll be putting on
a Fire performance.

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:29.710
Please be understanding...

00:11:30.840 --> 00:11:32.000
Rhyme...

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.420
I’m doing an
Electric performance here.

00:11:39.470 --> 00:11:41.260
Okay, I’ve got it.

00:11:41.260 --> 00:11:43.180
I don’t know if this will work,

00:11:43.180 --> 00:11:46.850
but try rehearsing with
your original partners.

00:11:46.850 --> 00:11:50.230
It’s bound to be <i>enchanting!</i>

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:53.440
I understand.

00:11:53.440 --> 00:11:55.240
I’ll give it a try.

00:11:55.240 --> 00:11:57.200
Hello!

00:11:57.200 --> 00:11:59.110
We hope you’ll look after us
again today!

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:04.200
Oh, welcome!

00:12:05.250 --> 00:12:05.910
Huh?

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:09.630
Ms. Honoka has Karen
with her, not Rhyme...

00:12:09.630 --> 00:12:11.040
You’re right.

00:12:11.040 --> 00:12:15.970
I decided they should practice with
their original partners, after all.

00:12:15.970 --> 00:12:17.300
But, you see...

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:25.100
Now!

00:12:32.820 --> 00:12:35.070
Electricity is pretty too,
but well...

00:12:43.240 --> 00:12:44.240
Come on!

00:12:52.080 --> 00:12:54.710
Fire is impressive too, but...

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:01.510
It’s not going very well.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:05.970
If they can’t work something out,
we might have to cancel the flying trapeze...

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:06.970
Whaa?!

00:13:06.970 --> 00:13:09.270
Cancel it right before
the show?!

00:13:09.270 --> 00:13:10.940
There’s no other option.

00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:16.730
I wouldn’t be satisfied, either,
if I had to put on a half-baked performance.

00:13:18.190 --> 00:13:19.320
I’m sorry.

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:21.660
None of this is your fault.

00:13:22.910 --> 00:13:24.700
I’m going to take a break.

00:13:32.250 --> 00:13:33.420
Ringleader.

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:34.880
I couldn’t help hearing...

00:13:34.880 --> 00:13:35.920
Right...

00:13:35.920 --> 00:13:37.590
With the way things are going...

00:13:38.010 --> 00:13:39.800
That might be the only choice.

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:43.090
This isn’t your fault.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:45.800
Sorry, I need a moment...

00:13:54.940 --> 00:13:56.360
Eevee!

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:01.320
Where could they have gone?

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:23.470
Are they training?

00:14:23.470 --> 00:14:25.340
Of course...

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:26.300
Huh?

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:30.350
They want to work together
to put on the show.

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.500
I wonder...
Does Eevee want to perform with them, too?

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:01.420
Looks like it.

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:02.800
That’s a great idea!

00:15:02.800 --> 00:15:04.970
Hey! Let us join in too!

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:09.010
Let’s practice together!

00:15:17.980 --> 00:15:19.310
Aw.

00:15:19.310 --> 00:15:23.030
A certain somebody
just <i>had</i> to ruin everything.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:25.070
That’s <i>my</i> line.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:27.820
If only my Rhyme
had become a Thunders...

00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:31.370
Same for Karen!
If only she evolved into Booster...

00:15:31.370 --> 00:15:32.290
Excuse me!

00:15:33.750 --> 00:15:36.540
Could you come with me?

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:38.500
There’s something
I’d like to show you.

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:42.130
Let’s go!

00:15:47.680 --> 00:15:50.220
Now, it’s my turn!
Come on!

00:15:54.350 --> 00:15:55.430
Karen...

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:56.940
Rhyme...

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:58.480
We’re not done yet!

00:16:01.440 --> 00:16:03.440
Here we go!

00:16:20.000 --> 00:16:21.750
Awesome!

00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:25.590
Rhyme...

00:16:25.590 --> 00:16:26.760
Karen...

00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:31.180
What’s going on?

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:34.260
Why are you
practicing together?

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.600
I think they’re doing it
for their partners.

00:16:37.270 --> 00:16:39.600
They want to be able to
perform for you,

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:43.150
so they’re working together,
and practicing as hard as they can.

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:45.570
Won’t you think of them, too,

00:16:45.570 --> 00:16:47.990
and figure out a way
to keep the act in?

00:16:59.210 --> 00:17:01.500
Karen... Thank you!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:03.590
You too, Rhyme... Thank you.

00:17:04.670 --> 00:17:06.880
These two are working so hard...

00:17:06.880 --> 00:17:09.300
...that we need to turn over
a new leaf, too!

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.760
Let’s work together...

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:13.550
...and put on a great show!

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:29.110
Now, our special guests today,

00:17:29.110 --> 00:17:33.490
Satoshi and Pikachu,
Go and Sarunori...

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:37.290
...make a <i>sparkling</i> entrance!

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.340
Let’s go, Pikachu!

00:17:54.930 --> 00:17:56.640
100,000 Volts!

00:18:03.520 --> 00:18:06.610
Sarunori, go! Branch Jab!

00:18:12.110 --> 00:18:13.610
We’ve got this, yeah!

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:14.360
All right!

00:18:14.820 --> 00:18:15.780
Pikachu!

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:32.510
The four of them were marvelous!

00:18:32.510 --> 00:18:33.970
Now, for the finale,

00:18:33.970 --> 00:18:37.140
we have Honoka and Thunders,
and Billy and Booster,

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:40.600
with their <i>enchanting</i>
flying trapeze act!

00:18:40.600 --> 00:18:46.360
And helping them out today,
we have Koharu and Eevee!

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:00.870
Here goes!

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:15.680
Rhyme!

00:19:16.430 --> 00:19:17.930
Karen!

00:19:23.180 --> 00:19:24.310
Beautiful!

00:19:24.310 --> 00:19:26.060
Amazing!

00:19:26.060 --> 00:19:28.440
Eevee, if you please!

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:46.370
That was incredible!

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:48.040
Bravo!

00:19:48.040 --> 00:19:49.420
Yes, yes!

00:19:49.420 --> 00:19:51.420
<i>Enchanting...</i>

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:12.770
Wasn’t that fun?

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:14.400
I wanna see it again!

00:20:15.780 --> 00:20:18.110
The show was a great success.

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:19.870
We had loads of fun!

00:20:19.870 --> 00:20:21.660
Thank you very much!

00:20:23.030 --> 00:20:26.460
Sorry for having you join us
on short notice, Koharu.

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:29.540
But the flying trapeze act
went wonderfully, thanks to you.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:30.210
Yeah.

00:20:30.210 --> 00:20:31.380
Don’t worry.

00:20:31.380 --> 00:20:33.840
I’m glad I got to perform!

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:36.260
I think Eevee enjoyed it, too!

00:20:37.880 --> 00:20:40.340
It’s not much,
but as a token of our gratitude...

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:42.680
...we want you to have these.

00:20:42.680 --> 00:20:43.760
Huh?

00:20:43.760 --> 00:20:45.060
Are those...?!

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:47.730
This is a Fire Stone...

00:20:47.730 --> 00:20:49.810
...and this is a Thunder Stone.

00:20:50.270 --> 00:20:54.230
Use them when it’s time
to evolve your Eevee.

00:20:56.360 --> 00:20:57.940
Thank you!

00:20:57.940 --> 00:21:00.860
And by all means,
make her a Thunders!

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:03.660
Electric types can be
surprisingly cool.

00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:07.870
I can recommend you
Booster, too.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:10.620
Fire types are amazing,
as well.

00:21:11.670 --> 00:21:12.790
Huh?

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:15.170
Something strange?

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:19.130
Our horizons have been broadened,
thanks to you.

00:21:19.670 --> 00:21:22.970
I wonder what Koharu’s Eevee’s
gonna evolve into!

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:24.760
I can’t wait to see!

00:21:26.520 --> 00:21:27.600
Eevee...

00:21:27.600 --> 00:21:31.100
Whatever you evolve into,
let’s always stay together!

00:21:34.230 --> 00:21:38.780
Koharu has learned of another kind of relationship
between Pokémon and Trainer.

00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:42.990
What kind of future could lie in store
for Koharu and Eevee?

00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:09.620
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.620 --> 00:23:10.910
Go!

00:23:12.700 --> 00:23:14.160
The Championships!

00:23:14.160 --> 00:23:16.500
My next battle’s in Galar!

00:23:18.500 --> 00:23:20.590
They’re rehearsing right now.

00:23:20.590 --> 00:23:22.090
Nobody may enter.

00:23:22.090 --> 00:23:24.760
Huh? Wasn’t this supposed
to be a Gym?

00:23:24.760 --> 00:23:26.890
I got skin in this game
too, y’know!

00:23:26.890 --> 00:23:28.850
I ain’t about to be goin’ down!

00:23:29.850 --> 00:23:31.890
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:31.890 --> 00:23:33.930
Mary from Spike Town!
